      "choiceType": null,
      "notes": [
        "The first year of Dutch Studies consists mainly of language acquisition courses. In the first semester English is used as a language of instruction; in the second semester all courses, except Humanities and the Digital World, are in Dutch. Apart from Dutch language acquisition, the first year consists of courses on Dutch art, culture, society, and linguistics. In the second semester students follow also The Netherlands in Dutch Feature Films. This course is an obligatory BSA course (please see the information on [BSA online](https://www.student.universiteitleiden.nl/en/study--studying/study/academic-progress/binding-study-advice/humanities/dutch-studies-ba?cf=humanities&cd=dutch-studies-ba)).\nThe timetables are avalable through [My Timetable](https://rooster.universiteitleiden.nl/schedule).\nDuring the first year the following activities are planned:\n\n* Introduction day, 4 hrs\n* Introduction session MyStudyMap, MyTimetable, Brightspace, website, Prospectus, 2 hrs\n* Introduction session Binding Study Advice 2 hrs\n* introduction session about the second term, 1 hour\n* introduction session about the second year and study plan, 2 hrs"
      ],
      "modules": []
    },
